# "During any turn you attacked with a Rogue" asks what the attacker was as it was declared (CR 508.1), not what it has
# become. Robber of the Rich attacks on turn 1 and exiles Lightning Bolt; after combat Turn to Frog makes it a Frog with no
# other creature type until end of turn. Bot1 still attacked with a Rogue this turn, so it casts the Bolt with Mox Pearl.
[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Robber of the Rich
Turn to Frog
Island
Island x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Lightning Bolt
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Robber of the Rich.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Robber of the Rich > Bot2)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Turn to Frog.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Robber of the Rich)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Robber of the Rich.Subtypes = Frog
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[Expect]
Turn = 1
Stack.Count = 0
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Life = 15
